$\tfrac{1}{2}$ is the **only** unit fraction equal to a half; $\tfrac{1}{3}, \tfrac{1}{4}, \dots$ are all smaller.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},x=6cm,y=1cm]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(1.1,0);
\draw (0,0.12)--(0,-0.12);
\draw (0.5,0.12)--(0.5,-0.12);
\draw (1,0.12)--(1,-0.12);
\node[below] at (0,-0.12) {$0$};
\node[below] at (0.5,-0.12) {$\frac12$};
\node[below] at (1,-0.12) {$1$};
\draw[|<->|] (0.02,0.2)--(0.48,0.2);
\node[above] at (0.25,0.3) {every $\frac1n$ with $n>2$ lies here};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The bars show one half and one fifth.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.65cm]
\foreach \i in {0,...,0} {\fill[blue!25] (\i,1.5) rectangle (\i+1,2.5);}
\draw (0,1.5) rectangle (2,2.5);
\foreach \i in {1,...,1} {\draw (\i,1.5)--(\i,2.5);}
\node[left] at (0,2) {$\frac12$};
\foreach \i in {0,...,0} {\fill[orange!30] (\i,0) rectangle (\i+1,1);}
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,1);
\foreach \i in {1,...,4} {\draw (\i,0)--(\i,1);}
\node[left] at (0,0.5) {$\frac15$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which shaded part is larger?
